<%#
  Shown on the first confirmation and on every later visit to the same link,
  and only the first sends the welcome email -- so nothing here promises one.
%>
<%# Own address carries a bearer token — see marketing.html.erb's use of this flag. %>
<% content_for :credential_page, true %>
<% content_for :title, "You're on the list — Remindly" %>

<h1>You're on the list</h1>

<p class="lead">
  Here is the routine sheet —
  <a href="<%= routine_sheet_path %>">open it and print it</a>. One page for
  the fridge door.
</p>

<p>
  The monthly note will arrive when there is one worth sending: one useful
  thing about caring for a parent at a distance, and a line on what has
  changed in Remindly. Every one of them has an unsubscribe link — or reply
  to come off the list, or write to
  <a href="mailto:hello@remindly.care">hello@remindly.care</a> if something
  looks wrong.
</p>

<div class="actions">
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= login_path %>">Try Remindly — it's free</a>
  <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="<%= blog_path %>">Read something first</a>
</div>
